Problem with Leaflet Proxy when the Leaflet Output object is not on the 1st selected tab. When the map tab is selected by the user, the Leaflet Output object is rendered, yet the Leaflet Proxy does not execute. The user must change an input for the markers to appear. Not sure if this is a Leaflet or a Shiny Issue. I am thinking that the observe function with the Leaflet Proxy tries to run before the Leaflet Output is rendered and thus fails.

REPREX:

```r
library(shiny)
library(leaflet)
library(RColorBrewer)

selected <- "Tab 1"
#selected <- "Map Tab"

ui <- fluidPage(
  tabsetPanel(
    tabPanel("Tab 1"),
    tabPanel("Map Tab",
             leafletOutput("map"),
             selectInput("colors", "Color Scheme",
                         rownames(subset(brewer.pal.info, category %in% c("seq", "div")))
             )
    ),
    selected = selected
  )
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {

  # Leaflet Output
  output$map <- renderLeaflet({
    leaflet(quakes) %>% addTiles() %>%
      fitBounds(~min(long), ~min(lat), ~max(long), ~max(lat))
  })
  
  colorpal <- reactive({
    colorNumeric(input$colors, quakes$mag)
